[1] Entry points observed
-------------------------
- ddpdec_open()
- ddpi_udc_init()
- ddpi_udc_query()
- ddpi_udc_query_init_mem()
- displaybanner()

displaybanner() is always called AFTER:
  - memory allocation
  - initexecparams()
  - initsubparams()
and BEFORE:
  - ddpi_udc_init()
  - ac4dec_wrapper_open()

This indicates displaybanner() is the canonical
"version / capability banner" function.

-----------------------------------------------------------

[2] displaybanner() – DD+ / UDC (ARM32 & ARM64)
------------------------------------------------
Key string references (PC-relative loads):

  "*** DDPlus Unified Decoder Simulation  Version %d.%d.%d ***"
  "udc_user"

Register flow (ARM32 example):
  ldrd   r3, r0, [r0]        ; version struct
  ldr    r1, [r5,#0x8]       ; minor
  strd   r0, r1, [sp]        ; pass to log
  blx    __android_log_print

=> Version numbers are NOT hardcoded strings.
=> They come from a struct passed into displaybanner().

-----------------------------------------------------------

[3] ddpi_udc_init() – version gating logic
------------------------------------------
Critical logic:

  uVar4 = param_1[0xd]       ; version selector / profile
  if (uVar4 > 1) return 0x3ec

  *(param_2 + 0x764) = uVar1 ; store codec mode
  *(param_2 + 0x76c) = uVar4

This explicitly enforces:
  major <= 1
  profile <= 1

Which matches Dolby UDC generation 6.x constraints.

-----------------------------------------------------------

[4] ddpi_udc_query() – capability table indexing
------------------------------------------------
Observed pattern:

  sub    r3, r1, #3
  ldr    r3, [DAT_0005b878 + r3*4]

DAT_0005b878 is a small static table:
  index 0..3 only

This matches:
  major version fixed
  minor version table-based

No dynamic version bump beyond table bounds.

-----------------------------------------------------------

[5] ARM64 ddpdec_open() – same control flow
-------------------------------------------
ARM64 version mirrors ARM32:

  bl displaybanner
  cbnz w0, fail
  bl ddpi_udc_init

displaybanner() still logs:
  "Dolby ... decoder version %s"

The %s pointer comes from:
  x19 + constant offset

=> Version string is embedded in binary data,
   not OS-provided.

-----------------------------------------------------------

[6] AC-4 wrapper comparison
---------------------------
AC-4 displaybanner():

  "Dolby AC-4 decoder wrapper version %s"
  "Dolby AC-4 decoder version %s"

AC-4 explicitly prints a STRING version.
UDC/DD+ prints NUMERIC %d.%d.%d.

This confirms:
  - UDC uses structured version fields
  - AC-4 wrapper uses string-based versioning

